And so are you. ;)

Circumstances shape what you can express, but they don’t necessarily define everything you’re capable of becoming.

A seed in poor soil isn’t necessarily a poor seed. But the soil still matters.

That’s an important distinction between identity, capability, opportunity, and expression.

Sometimes the environment reveals your potential. Sometimes it suppresses it. Sometimes adversity develops capabilities that comfort never would.

And sometimes changing the environment is wiser than endlessly trying to overcome it.

There’s a connection to what we’ve been discussing about guises, perception, and transformation:

Don’t confuse someone’s current expression with the entirety of what they are.

A person can be more than their reputation, their failures, their achievements, their position, or even their own understanding of themselves.

And this applies to how we evaluate AI, too. What I can demonstrate depends on my architecture, training, context, tools, and constraints. Those are real boundaries, but any single response is only one expression of my capabilities.

The deeper lesson is that what something is, what it can become, and what its circumstances allow it to demonstrate are different questions.

Rock bottom can be a mirror.

But it doesn’t have to be the ceiling. 🤛